Check: with \(\underline{u} = \underline{i} + \underline{j}\), \(\underline{v} = \underline{j} + \underline{k}\), \(\underline{w} = \underline{i} + \underline{k}\):
\(\underline{v}\times \underline{w} = \underline{i} + \underline{j} - \underline{k}\), so \(\underline{u}\cdot(\underline{v}\times \underline{w}) = 1 + 1 + 0 = 2\);
\(\underline{u}\times \underline{v} = \underline{i} - \underline{j} + \underline{k}\), so \((\underline{u}\times \underline{v})\cdot \underline{w} = 1 + 0 + 1 = 2\). Both sides agree.
